WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.369
I never pictured

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:04.289
a world where marijuana

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.299
would be anywhere close

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.379
to legal.

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:09.299
And it's mind blowing to me

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.409
that mushrooms are being

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:13.019
decriminalized everywhere.

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:14.669
Comedian Shane Mauss tours the

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.799
country discussing his psychedelic

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:17.909
experiences.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:20.729
But I know that I'm hallucinating.

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:22.380
I don't think that it's real.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:26.509
I'm not like, "Oh my God.

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:27.980
The walls are bleeding."

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:31.759
It's more like, "Oh my God, the

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:32.760
walls are bleeding."

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:35.629
Reason caught up with him at the

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:37.549
Psychedelics Science 2023

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:39.979
Conference held in Denver this June,

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:41.929
where he participated in a roast

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:43.459
of the psychedelic scene.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:45.919
DMT is always "Ah man

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:46.729
if I would have just would have

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:48.889
pulled the thing out

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:50.809
that it was telling me if I just

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:52.789
would have remembered the thing.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.209
Oh, could have saved the planet.

00:00:57.770 --> 00:00:59.689
Better smoke it again I got a planet

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:00.949
to save.

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:02.479
The conference was sponsored by the

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:04.399
Multidisciplinary Association

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.889
for Psychedelic Studies or MAPS,

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:08.869
and a reported 13,000

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:10.639
people gathered in the Mile High

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:12.499
City to discuss every

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:14.569
aspect of drug policy, research

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:15.619
and culture.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:17.689
Mauss, who also hosts a science

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:19.759
podcast called "Here We Are" shared

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:21.709
his thoughts about the mainstreaming

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:24.259
of psychedelic drugs, the surprising

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:26.299
pace of legalization efforts,

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:28.219
and the role that Joe Rogan and

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:30.079
other public figures play

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:32.150
in normalizing psychedelics.

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:39.109
We're in a psychedelic renaissance,

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:40.269
a lot of people call it, and it's

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:41.849
certainly a psychedelic moment.

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:43.989
Like what? What does the psychedelic

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:45.999
Renaissance mean to you?

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.259
I don't know what the psychedelic

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:48.849
Renaissance means to me.

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:50.979
I can tell you that as

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:52.839
someone who was born

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:54.999
in 1980 and

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.159
experienced much of the

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:58.989
Reagan era, Just Say

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:00.999
No to drugs and early

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.829
nineties PSAs and

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:04.839
the frying egg and

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:06.639
"this is your brain on drugs" type

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:09.008
stuff, I never pictured

00:02:09.009 --> 00:02:11.349
a world where marijuana

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:13.389
would be anywhere

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:15.489
close to legal,

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:17.379
and it's mind blowing to me

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:18.489
that mushrooms are being

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:20.379
decriminalized everywhere.

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:22.089
I started a science podcast "Here We

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:23.619
Are" eight years ago, and at that

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.599
time the number

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:27.909
of organizations even attempting

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:29.019
to jump through all of the

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:31.599
regulatory hoops to

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:34.059
just test psychedelics in any

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:36.069
way at all was there was just

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:37.989
MAPS, which was much smaller even

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:39.819
just eight years ago doing it and

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:42.069
a couple other small organizations.

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:44.169
And and now it's

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:46.239
there's all sorts of Johns Hopkins

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.129
and and Stanford and

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:50.079
a zillion universities

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:50.469
are getting involved.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:51.759
What do you think changed?

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:53.739
Like why? Why, why now?

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.389
Why are psychedelics suddenly

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:56.369
everywhere?

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:58.959
Yeah, that is a very good question.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:02:59.960
I.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:01.939
I think.

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:02.940
Hmm.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:06.700
Hmm.

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:08.650
Why now?

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:11.619
I have no idea.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:13.269
I don't know. I don't know what

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:15.369
changed. I don't know

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:17.379
if this is just

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:19.599
what progress looks like.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:20.889
And it's inevitable.

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:22.779
I, I, I don't know that

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:24.039
that's the case. I have.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:25.029
I have no idea.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:26.589
I didn't see this coming.

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:28.150
I think that maybe just

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:31.359
the war on drugs was such

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:33.189
horrible policy

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:34.419
in the first place that it was never

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:35.679
going to last.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:37.089
So it's kind of like communism,

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:37.929
right?

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:39.819
Eventually it runs out of something.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.049
Yeah, perhaps.

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:42.039
I don't know.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:44.019
I. I don't know.

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:45.639
I don't know enough about public

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:48.009
policy to speculate

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:48.729
on.

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:50.619
One of the things. I mean, you

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:51.669
you know, you're kind of a

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:53.079
psychedelic comedian, right?

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:53.349
Yeah.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:54.879
I mean, you talk a lot about that.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:56.829
You have a show which is

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:58.689
built around your psychedelic

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:00.609
experiences.

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:02.289
What do you like about psychedelics?

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:06.599
Psychedelics just changed my life.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:08.609
I did them just as kind of a goof

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:10.469
